<h2>Per-Site Methods</h2>
<div class="indented">
        <p>
            Each of these methods operates on a single site at a time, identified by the <code>site</code> parameter. This parameter can be the full domain name (ie. "stackoverflow.com"),
            or a short form identified by <code>api_site_parameter</code> on the <a href="/docs/types/site">site object</a>.
        </p>

    <h3>Answers</h3>
    <div class="indented">
                <div class="method">
            <div class="method-name">
                <a href="/docs/answers">answers</a>
            </div>
            <div class="method-description">
                Get all answers on the site.
            </div>
            <br class="csp-clear" />
        </div>

                <div class="method">
            <div class="method-name">
                <a href="/docs/answers-by-ids">answers/{ids}</a>
            </div>
            <div class="method-description">
                Get answers identified by a set of ids.
            </div>
            <br class="csp-clear" />
        </div>


                <div class="method">
            <div class="method-name">
                <a href="/docs/accept-answer">answers/{id}/accept</a>
            </div>
            <div class="method-description">
                Casts an accept vote on the given answer.
                    <span class="need-auth" title="this method requires an access_token">auth required</span>
            </div>
            <br class="csp-clear" />
        </div>

